hat it's going to be  done manually and then you can go into  the  dashboard where you approve apps and you  would have to approve it in there  it can also be done through an api okay  i'll take  two more and then we'll wrap up can  apogee leverage cloud functions  or use a cloud function as the back-end  api source can it use pub sub for  queuing  so yes absolutely so a few different  ways to do this  um we've got some um we've got some  connectors that are  in apogee for google cloud platform so  if you're working on google cloud  platform you'll find built-in support  for this  if you happen to be working on aws or  another cloud  check our documentation for that there  are some examples of doing  lambda functions or um in other cases  as long as something has an api or  that can be connected to through http  this is going to be pretty easy to do  what's the preferred approach to  restrict access to apis protected by  apogee so traffic must go through apogee  first  firewall rules tls certificates um how  do we do that  so yes firewall rules and tls  certificates uh  would be two ways to do that but  basically  some form of cutting off access that  doesn't go through apogee and that's  typically done through  through networking techniques all right  our next webcast coming up on january  17th  is hybrid apps migration and  modernization and the need for api  management  thank you for attending today and happy  new year to everyone out there from  everyone at apogee  you
 

